<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Civilista Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1871</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Civilista Party was a Peruvian political party founded in 1871 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuel-pardo">Manuel Pardo</a>, the country's first organised civilian party, representing merchants, financiers and coastal landowners opposed to military rule. Pardo became its first president in 1872, and the party dominated government during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aristocratic-republic">Aristocratic Republic</a> from 1895 to 1919. It declined after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augusto-b-leguia">Augusto B. Leguía</a>'s coup of 1919.</p></div>
